{
  "_comment": [
    "The single definition of every bot action and its parameters.",
    "The interpreter reads parameters only through this file (carpet.logic.program.ActionSchema), and the web",
    "editor builds its node widgets from it and compiles graphs against it (webui/js/node-compiler.js).",
    "kind: action (a step), control (holds other actions in the listed slots) or condition (tested by IF_THEN_ELSE",
    "and by WAIT_UNTIL). A condition may hold conditions of its own: one in 'condition', or a list in 'conditions'.",
    "BREAK and CONTINUE belong inside a loop (LOOP, FOREVER, WHILE, FOR_EACH) and are refused anywhere else. They",
    "and STOP_PROGRAM are control actions without a slot: nothing in their own sequence runs after them.",
    "node: the editor node this action is compiled from.",
    "params: name, type (int, number, bool, string, expr), default, and optionally min/max or the allowed options.",
    "An int or number parameter may also hold an expression as text, of which a variable, the referencePrefix",
    "followed by a name as in '$counter', is the simplest. A variable that was never set reads as 0.",
    "A string parameter holds at most 1024 characters, or its maxLength. code: scarpet marks one that holds Scarpet.",
    "unbudgeted: the action runs Scarpet, which the per-tick budget cannot interrupt; it is charged a fixed number of steps.",
    "An expr parameter always holds an expression; returns says what it has to give: bool, number, text, list or any.",
    "requires: the boolean carpet rule that must be on for the action to work.",
    "drivesBody: the action moves the bot or clicks for it. While a combat node owns the bot the interpreter skips",
    "these, so that the combat brain is the only thing driving the action pack.",
    "optionsFrom: the allowed values are taken from the running server instead of being written here: 'combatStyles'",
    "are the combat styles /bot spawn takes and 'difficulties' its five difficulty presets.",
    "A 'ticks' parameter is how long the step lasts before the next one starts.",
    "ON_EVENT registers a reaction and then carries on with the sequence: its children run when the event happens,",
    "taking over from the main sequence, which resumes where it was once they are done. Every event fires on its",
    "rising edge only, and an event that fires while its own handler is still running is ignored.",
    "expressions: the vocabulary of the expression language (carpet.logic.program.Expression, webui/js/expression.js): the named",
    "values and the functions an expression may use. cost is the steps a call is charged (1 when absent); a variadic function's params are the required leading ones."
  ],
  "variables": {
    "referencePrefix": "$",
    "namePattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$",
    "maxVariables": 64
  },
  "expressions": {
    "values": [
      {"name": "health", "type": "number", "description": "The bot's health points; 20 is a full bar."},
      {"name": "max_health", "type": "number", "description": "The most health points the bot can have."},
      {"name": "food", "type": "number", "description": "The bot's food level; 20 is full."},
      {"name": "armor", "type": "number", "description": "How many armor points the bot is wearing."},
      {"name": "x", "type": "number", "description": "The bot's east-west position."},
      {"name": "y", "type": "number", "description": "The bot's height."},
      {"name": "z", "type": "number", "description": "The bot's north-south position."},
      {"name": "yaw", "type": "number", "description": "The way the bot faces, left to right, in degrees."},
      {"name": "pitch", "type": "number", "description": "How far the bot looks up or down, in degrees."},
      {"name": "held_count", "type": "number", "description": "How many items are in the bot's main hand."},
      {"name": "hotbar_slot", "type": "number", "description": "The hotbar slot the bot has selected, 1 to 9."},
      {"name": "target_distance", "type": "number", "description": "How far away the bot's target is; infinity when it has none."},
      {"name": "target_health", "type": "number", "description": "The target's health points; infinity when there is no target."},
      {"name": "tick", "type": "number", "description": "How many ticks have passed since the program started."},
      {"name": "random", "type": "number", "description": "A new random number from 0 up to, but not including, 1 each time it is read."},
      {"name": "held_item", "type": "text", "description": "The id of the item in the main hand, like diamond_sword; air when empty."},
      {"name": "offhand_item", "type": "text", "description": "The id of the item in the off hand; air when empty."},
      {"name": "target_held_item", "type": "text", "description": "The id of the item the target holds; air when there is no target."},
      {"name": "target_name", "type": "text", "description": "The target's name; empty when there is no target."},
      {"name": "bot_name", "type": "text", "description": "The bot's own name."},
      {"name": "on_ground", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot stands on the ground."},
      {"name": "in_water", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot is in water."},
      {"name": "gliding", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot is flying with an elytra."},
      {"name": "blocking", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot is raising a shield."},
      {"name": "using_item", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot is eating, drawing a bow or using another item."},
      {"name": "sprinting", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot is sprinting."},
      {"name": "sneaking", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot is sneaking."},
      {"name": "alive", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the bot is alive."},
      {"name": "has_target", "type": "bool", "description": "True when the bot has someone to fight."},
      {"name": "fighting", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the combat AI is on and the bot has a target it is engaging."},
      {"name": "target_blocking", "type": "bool", "description": "True while the target is raising a shield."}
    ],
    "functions": [
      {"name": "min", "params": [{"name": "a", "type": "number"}, {"name": "b", "type": "number"}], "variadic": true, "returns": "number", "description": "The smallest of two or more numbers."},
      {"name": "max", "params": [{"name": "a", "type": "number"}, {"name": "b", "type": "number"}], "variadic": true, "returns": "number", "description": "The largest of two or more numbers."},
      {"name": "abs", "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "description": "A number without its minus sign."},
      {"name": "floor", "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "description": "A number rounded down to a whole number."},
      {"name": "ceil", "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "description": "A number rounded up to a whole number."},
      {"name": "round", "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "description": "A number rounded to the nearest whole number; halves go up."},
      {"name": "sqrt", "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "description": "The square root of a number that is not negative."},
      {"name": "clamp", "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "number"}, {"name": "low", "type": "number"}, {"name": "high", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "description": "A number held between a lowest and a highest value."},
      {"name": "if", "params": [{"name": "condition", "type": "bool"}, {"name": "then", "type": "any"}, {"name": "otherwise", "type": "any"}], "returns": "any", "description": "The second value when the condition is true, otherwise the third; only the one that is used is worked out."},
      {"name": "len", "params": [{"name": "value", "type": "any"}], "returns": "number", "description": "How many characters a text has, or how many items a list has."},
      {"name": "contains", "params": [{"name": "value", "type": "any"}, {"name": "item", "type": "any"}], "returns": "bool", "description": "True when a text holds a piece of text, or a list holds an item."},
      {"name": "get", "params": [{"name": "list", "type": "list"}, {"name": "index", "type": "number"}], "returns": "any", "description": "The item at a place in a list; the first item is at 0."},
      {"name": "list", "params": [], "variadic": true, "returns": "list", "description": "Makes a list out of any number of values."},
      {"name": "range", "params": [{"name": "n", "type": "number"}], "returns": "list", "description": "The whole numbers from 0 up to one less than n, as a list."},
      {"name": "text", "params": [{"name": "value", "type": "any"}], "returns": "text", "description": "Any value written out as text."},
      {"name": "number", "params": [{"name": "value", "type": "any"}], "returns": "number", "description": "A number, or text that holds a number, as a number."},
      {"name": "distance", "params": [{"name": "x", "type": "number"}, {"name": "y", "type": "number"}, {"name": "z", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "cost": 1, "description": "How far the bot is from a spot in the world."},
      {"name": "player_distance", "params": [{"name": "name", "type": "text"}], "returns": "number", "cost": 2, "description": "How far the bot is from the named player."},
      {"name": "count", "params": [{"name": "item", "type": "text"}], "returns": "number", "cost": 2, "description": "How many of an item the bot carries."},
      {"name": "block", "params": [{"name": "x", "type": "number"}, {"name": "y", "type": "number"}, {"name": "z", "type": "number"}], "returns": "text", "cost": 5, "description": "The id of the block at a spot in the world."},
      {"name": "entities", "params": [{"name": "type", "type": "text"}, {"name": "radius", "type": "number"}], "returns": "number", "cost": 20, "description": "How many entities of a type are within a radius of the bot."}
    ]
  },
